    key_formulas: '• Pythagoras: Hypotenuse² = Opp² + Adj² (c² = a² + b²)\n• SOH CAH TOA: sin θ = Opp/Hyp, cos θ = Adj/Hyp, tan θ = Opp/Adj\n• Sine Rule: a/sin A = b/sin B = c/sin C\n• Cosine Rule: a² = b² + c² - 2bc cos A\n• Special Angles: sin 30° = cos 60° = 0.5 | tan 45° = 1 | sin 45° = 1/√2',
    pro_tips_95: 'WAEC Chief Examiner Secret: Use the Sine Rule when given 2 angles and 1 side (or 2 sides and opposite angle). Use the Cosine Rule when given 3 sides or 2 sides and included angle!',
