    content: `<p>Today we will learn about how to calculate profit and loss percentages. These calculations help us understand how much money we make or lose when we buy and sell items.</p><h2 style="text-align:center"><strong>What is Profit and Loss?</strong></h2><p><strong>Profit</strong>: When you sell something for more than what you paid for it, you make a profit.</p><p><strong>Loss</strong>: When you sell something for less than what you paid for it, you incur a loss.</p><h2 style="text-align:center"><strong>Formulas</strong></h2><p>Here are some important formulas to remember:</p><p>1. <strong> Profit</strong>:</p><p>2. <strong> Loss</strong>:</p><p>3. Percentage Profit:</p><p>4. Percentage Loss:</p><h2><strong>Examples</strong></h2><p><strong>Example 1</strong> : Calculating Percentage Profit</p><p>Adamu bought a bicycle for ₦25,000 and sold it for ₦30,000. What is his percentage profit?</p><p>Solution:</p><p>1. Calculate the profit:</p><p>2. Calculate the percentage profit:</p><p>So, Adamu's percentage profit is 20%.</p><p><strong>Example 2</strong> : Calculating Percentage Loss</p><p>Derinde bought a carton of sugar for ₦4,200. There are 12 packets in the carton, and he sold each packet for ₦320. What is the selling price of the carton, the loss, and the percentage loss?</p><p>Solution:</p><p>1. Calculate the selling price of the carton:</p><p>2. Calculate the loss:</p><p>3. Calculate the percentage loss:</p><p>So, Derinde's percentage loss is approximately 8.57%.</p><p><strong>Example 3:</strong> Another Percentage Loss Calculation</p><p>Calculate the percentage loss on an article bought for ₦9,000 and sold for ₦8,280.</p><p>Solution:</p><p>1. Calculate the loss:</p><p>2. Calculate the percentage loss:</p><p>So, the percentage loss is approximately 8%.</p><h2><strong>Practice Questions</strong></h2><ol><li>John bought a toy for ₦500 and sold it for ₦650. What is his percentage profit?</li><li>Mary sold a book for ₦1,200 which she bought for ₦1,500. Calculate her percentage loss.</li><li>A vendor bought a batch of fruits for ₦2,000 and sold them for ₦2,400. Find the percentage profit.</li><li>If a shopkeeper buys a shirt for ₦800 and sells it for ₦720, what is his percentage loss?</li></ol>`
