    summary_60s: 'A matrix is a rectangular array of numbers, symbols, or expressions arranged in rows and columns, denoted by a capital letter (e.g., A). The order of a matrix specifies its dimensions, specifically the number of rows and columns it contains. Rows are the horizontal lines of eleme',
    key_formulas: '• Linear Form: ax + b = 0 ⇒ x = -b/a\n• Difference of Two Squares: a² - b² = (a - b)(a + b)\n• Perfect Square: (a ± b)² = a² ± 2ab + b²\n• Remainder Theorem: P(x) ÷ (x - c) ⇒ Remainder = P(c)',
