    summary_60s: 'An inequality is a mathematical statement in which two expressions are compared using inequality symbols rather than an equals sign. The inequality sign communicates whether one quantity is less than , greater than , less than or equal to , greater than or equal to , or simply no',
    key_formulas: '• Linear Form: ax + b = 0 ⇒ x = -b/a\n• Difference of Two Squares: a² - b² = (a - b)(a + b)\n• Perfect Square: (a ± b)² = a² ± 2ab + b²\n• Remainder Theorem: P(x) ÷ (x - c) ⇒ Remainder = P(c)',
    pro_tips_95: 'WAEC Examiner Trap: When expanding -(a - b), the minus sign distributes to BOTH terms to give -a + b. In JAMB, factorize common algebraic factors before cross-multiplying!',
    syllabus_objectives: 'Candidates should be able to master the fundamental principles of Inequalities (Algebra) in line with the official syllabus.',
