    key_formulas: '• AP nth Term: T_n = a + (n - 1)d\n• AP Sum: S_n = n/2 [2a + (n - 1)d] = n/2 (a + l)\n• GP nth Term: T_n = a·rⁿ⁻¹\n• GP Sum: S_n = a(1 - rⁿ) / (1 - r) [|r| < 1]\n• Sum to Infinity: S_∞ = a / (1 - r)',
    pro_tips_95: 'WAEC Scoring Tip: Always write out the first 3 terms of an AP/GP to verify your first term (a) and common difference (d) or common ratio (r) before substituting into formulas!',
    syllabus_objectives: 'Candidates should be able to master the fundamental principles of Equilibrium of a Rigid Body in line with the official syllabus.',
    updated_at: 'JAMB • WAEC Official Syllabus',
    content: `<p><strong>5. Equilibrium of a Rigid Body</strong></p>
<p>Moment of inertia, radius of gyration, parallel and perpendicular axes theorems, and kinetic energy of a rotating body in simple cases.</p>`
