    summary_60s: 'In geometry, a locus (plural: loci) is the set of all points that satisfy a specific condition or set of conditions. Common Types Of Loci Perpendicular bisector locus Locus of points at a given distance from a straight line Locus of points at a given distance from a fixed point A',
